CI note (updated — I've now traced the cause rather than just asserting it wasn't this branch).

The red is `General tests (server (2/5))`, failing on `workspace-runtime.test.ts > requires Paperclip dev runtime services to pass /api/health readiness`. `verify` is only the roll-up gate reporting it, so there is one failure, not two.

It is a bug in the readiness reporting path on `master`, not in this branch. In `server/src/services/workspace-runtime.ts` the loop is entered while any time remains, and the probe's `AbortSignal` is clamped to whatever is left:

```js
while (now() < deadline) {
  const probeBudgetMs = Math.max(1, Math.min(RUNTIME_SERVICE_READINESS_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS, deadline - now()));
  try {
    const response = await fetchImpl(readinessUrl, { signal: AbortSignal.timeout(probeBudgetMs) });
    if (response.ok) return;
    lastError = `received HTTP ${response.status}`;
  } catch (err) {
    lastError = err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err);
  }
```

A probe admitted with a millisecond left aborts immediately, and the `catch` overwrites `lastError`, discarding the `503` an earlier probe observed. The test asserts `received HTTP 503` and gets `The operation was aborted`, which is exactly the CI output. Whether it lands that way depends on where the final iteration falls relative to the deadline, which is why it is intermittent.

