Three escape paths kept from yours; `master`'s version named two.

Nothing else changed. `ui` typecheck clean, full `ui` suite **4014 pass** — the one failure, `IssueProperties`, is timezone-dependent and reproduces on `master`.

**One thing worth a second look before this merges**, from the session that did the `InviteLanding` sibling: it recommended `removeQueries` over `resetQueries`, on the grounds that reset keeps the query object and can leave existing observers reading `isFetchedAfterMount: false` afterward. Your reasoning for `resetQueries` — that `removeQueries` does not notify mounted observers, and `CompanyProvider` stays mounted across the whole cycle — is specific and looks right to me for that case.

The live consumer of that flag is `AppsConnect.tsx:374-375`, which sits behind the `apps/connect` route and so should unmount on sign-out, which would make the concern moot. I have not verified that unmount actually happens — I inferred it from the route table — so I would treat it as likely fine rather than settled. Note the onboarding gate no longer reads `isFetchedAfterMount` at all; #11382 removed it in favour of `isSuccess`.
